{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>נטף.</b> It is צֳרִי, and because it is nothing but the sap that drips from the trees of the ketoret it is called נָטָף; וּבְלַעַז גומ\"א, and what is called צֳרִי they call טרי\"אקה." "<b>ושחלת.</b> A root of a spice, smooth and glossy like a fingernail; in Mishnaic language it is called צִפֹרֶן — and this is what Onkelos rendered: וְטוּפְרָא." "<b>וחלבנה.</b> A spice whose odor is foul, and they call it גַלְבְּנָא. Scripture counts it among the ingredients of the ketaret to teach us that we should not take it lightly to include with us in the bundle of our fasts and our prayers the sinners of Israel, that they be counted with us." "<b>סמים.</b> Others." "<b>ולבנה זכה.</b> From here our Sages learned: eleven ingredients were stated to Moses at Sinai — the minimum of סַמִּים is two; נָטָף and שְׁחֵלֶת and חֶלְבְּנָה are three — that makes five; סַמִּים to include as many more — that makes ten; and לְבוֹנָה — that makes eleven. And these are they: הַצֳרִי, הַצִפֹרֶן, הַחֶלְבְּנָה, הַלְּבוֹנָה, מֹר, קְצִיעָה, שִׁבֹּלֶת נֵרְדְּ, כַרְכֹּם — that makes eight — for שִׁבֹּלֶת and נֵרְדְּ are one, for נֵרְדְּ resembles שִׁבֹּלֶת; הַקֹּשְׁטְ, הַקִּלּוּפָה, קִנָּמוֹן — that makes eleven; בֹּרִית כַרְשִׁינָה — it is not offered as incense but only to rub the צִפֹרֶן to whiten it so it be fine (Keritot 6)." "<b>בד בבד יהיה.</b> These four mentioned here shall be equal, weight for weight — the weight of this one like the weight of that one. And thus we learned: הַצֳּרִי וְהַצִּפֹּרֶן הַחֶלְבְּנָה וְהַלְּבוֹנָה, weight of seventy, seventy maneh (ibid.). And the term בַּד appears to me to be in the singular: one by one they shall be — this equal to this."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {4 "la'az גומ\"א (comment 0) is Old French gomme, 'gum'; טרי\"אקה Old French triaque, 'theriac'."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:04.604773448Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}